From 8ede4412b3dc33b4bf5071bed3d38bdac55921fc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rakibul Islam <33988342+raykibul@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 00:44:18 +0600
Subject: [PATCH 2/8] feat(desktop): complete the composer's directory against
 the filesystem
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The recents list and the search were one control doing two jobs, and it
could only ever do the first. `ListDirectories` returns the distinct CWDs
that already have a session, so a directory nobody has worked in yet was
unreachable — the list said "these are your options" and meant it.

Typing now completes against the disk. The typed path is split at its
last separator, the parent is listed through GET /api/files, and the
directories in it whose name starts with the rest are offered under a
section naming where they came from. A bare or relative path completes
under home, which is where a session with no directory starts anyway.
Tab fills in the top match, as a shell does.

The recents keep their own section above that, tinted and counted as
before. They are the answer to "back to where I was working", which
completion is not, and they are the only rows that can carry a project
name or say what is running there.

And the escape hatch the free-text input had is back: whatever is in the
box is committable as it stands, absolute or not, on Enter or on the row
at the top. A path this end has never heard of — a fresh checkout, a
mount, a directory made a second ago — must not need the list's
agreement. Two more losses go with it: the typed path is held by the
dialog rather than by the popover, so it survives the chip closing, and
Home stays on the list while it is being spelled.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
